  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46270\", \"PowerToys#47576\"], \"answer\": \"This looks like the known Dock bug where bookmark bands don't render their icon or name. No past ticket describes the add (+) picker specifically, so the match is close but not exact. PowerToys#46270 is the tracking issue. In 0.100.0 a maintainer said a fix PR existed but hadn't been merged, so 0.100.x doesn't include it. Try these workarounds from that ticket. (1) In Command Palette, disable and then re-enable the Bookmarks extension, or reload extensions. (2) Turn on Settings > General > For Developers > 'Enable External reload'. Then run x-cmdpal://reload, for example from a .vbs file that you pin as a bookmark or put in shell:startup. Bookmarks should then show again. Update PowerToys once a release containing the fix is available, and subscribe to #46270 for updates. If the picker still shows blank entries after a reload, add that to #46270.\"}",
